problem_statement:
[feature request] move const to impl
It would be cool if we could have an assist that would do the following transformation:

```rust
struct Foo;

impl Foo {
    fn test(&self) -> usize {
        /// A doc comment attached.
        const XY$0Z: usize = 1234;
        
        XYZ
    }   
}
```

Into:

```rust

struct Foo;

impl Foo {
    /// A doc comment attached.
    const XYZ: usize = 1234;
    
    fn test(&self) -> usize {
        Self::XYZ
    } 
}
```

Add mechanism to disable rules inline within a given block.
The current implementation of `<!-- template-lint disabled=true -->` or `<!-- template-lint bare-strings=false -->` disables the rule for the entire "rest" of the template they are in. We should add a better control/configuration system so that it is possible to disable all or a single rule within a given block.

The principle behind this (i.e. how we think of it applying to the DOM tree) is that we're providing two ways of configuring the linter in a template:

1. Add an instruction as an in element comment (`<div {{! template-lint`) that applies to it and (optionally) to its descendants.
2. Add an instruction as a child-less node (`{{! template-lint`) that applies to all of its later siblings nodes and (mandatorily) to their descendants.

```hbs
<div>
  {{! template-lint disabled=true }}
  {{! Things are disabled here }}
</div>
{{! But not disabled here }}
```

```hbs
{{#foo-bar as |baz|}}
  {{! template-lint invalid-interactive=false }}
  {{! invalid-interactive is disabled here }}
{{/foo-bar}}
{{! invalid-interactive is reset to its original / global configuration here }}
```

```hbs
<div>
  <div {{! template-lint rule='invalid-interactive' disabled=true}}>
    {{! invalid-interactive *not* disabled }}
  </div>
</div>
```

```hbs
<div>
  <div {{! template-lint rule='invalid-interactive' disabled=true recursive=true}}>
    {{! invalid-interactive *is* disabled }}
  </div>
</div>
```


<details>
  <summary>Original Proposal</summary>

Off the top of my head, I would like to add something like:

``` hbs
{{#template-lint disabled=true}}
  {{! Things are disabled here }}
{{/template-lint}}

{{! But not disabled here }}
```

These `{{template-lint` component invocations would be completely removed at build time (just like the HTML comments are today). This would also allow us to slowly phase out the current usage of HTML comments, which is somewhat odd anyways. 

Here is an early mockup of what this might look like: http://rwjblue.jsbin.com/vayamom/edit?html,js,output
</details>

Injection of parameterized types doesn't work as expected
Hi everyone, I expericene a problem with injecting parameterized types. It seems avaje-inject is not able to find beans, if they have a type parameter even though the bean is present in the bean scope. For example I tried to define a bean of [MongoCollection](https://mongodb.github.io/mongo-java-driver/4.11/apidocs/mongodb-driver-sync/com/mongodb/client/MongoCollection.html) in a `@Factory` annotated configuration class via a `@Bean` annotated factory method:

```java
@Factory
class MyConfig {

    @Bean
    public MongoCollection<MyDocument> buildCollection() {
        // omitted for brevity
    }
}
```

Then I tried to inject the bean into my component test (I tried both using `@InjectTest` as well as programmatically creating the `BeanScope`).

The run fails with: `No bean found for type: ...` even though I can see the bean in the BeanScop, when debugging.

I was able to work around this issue by using the raw type in the definition of the factory method as well as when injecting the bean, but I'd rather not be forced to cast the object everytime:

```java
@Factory
class MyConfig {

    @Bean
    public MongoCollection buildCollection() {
        // omitted for brevity
    }
}
```

Did I miss something? Is this really the intended behavior?

