ABCs for Devices that implement the "Bluesky Interface"
@untzag and @ksunden have suggested adding some ABCs for the expected Bluesky Interfaces. ABCs would be a useful tool for scaffolding implementations of the Readble, Movable, and Flyable interfaces. I would want to avoid accidentally giving the impression that implementation _must_ subclass from them. A key selling point for Bluesky is that other libraries can implement its interfaces and be interoperable without a software dependency. In our documentation, we should emphasize that they are optional, to be used or referred to if they help, or ignored otherwise.

We should also be sure that these ABCs implement https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html#abc.ABCMeta.__subclasshook__ so that they will behave correctly if `isinstance` is used.

PhpUnitDedicateAssertFixer is replacing functions with deprecated/removed method names of PHPUnit v9.1+
### Problem description

Since PHPUnit version 9.1 some of the dedicated asserts methods are renamed to a more readable name.
E.g. assertDirectoryNotExists() is renamed to assertDirectoryDoesNotExists()
(see list on https://github.com/sebastianbergmann/phpunit/blob/9.1.0/ChangeLog-9.1.md)
Since PHPUnit version 10 these deprecated methods are removed.

The PhpUnitDedicateAssertFixer is still referencing to the old names 
https://github.com/PHP-CS-Fixer/PHP-CS-Fixer/blob/master/src/Fixer/PhpUnit/PhpUnitDedicateAssertFixer.php.
So when i'm using PHPUnit version 10+ the fixer will break my code.
