protoparse: does not check for unique json_name in proto3 files
This is a case where protoparse accepts a proto source file that protoc rejects.

When a file uses `syntax = "proto3"`, protoc _requires_ that all fields have unique JSON names. So if the fields all collide on the same camel-case name (which is how protoc computes the JSON name from the proto field name), it complains:

```proto
// test.proto
syntax = "proto3";
message Foo {
  string bar = 1;
  string _Bar = 2;
}
```

Compiling with protoc yields this:
```
test.proto:5:10: The JSON camel-case name of field "_Bar" conflicts with field "bar". This is not allowed in proto3.
```

But protoparse does not perform this validation.

Note that protoparse should implement the checks _correctly_ and _not_ try to reproduce known bugs in protoc (https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/issues/5063 and https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/issues/7192)
(Which means protoparse will intentionally diverge from protoc behavior until these bugs are fixed.)

