Decide what to do with `keyof` expressions
I have some code samples like this in _Effective TypeScript_:

```ts
interface Options {
  width: number;
  height: number;
  color: string;
  label: string;
}

type OptionsKeys = keyof Options;
// Type is "width" | "height" | "color" | "label"
```

This stopped working as of [TS 4.2] when the type started displaying as `type OptionsKey = keyof Options`. I [don't like this][1], think it's [a bug][3] and have [written about it][2] but it seems like this change is here to stay. literate-ts needs some way to handle it.

