Process leak if cgroup init process shares process namespace
The cgroup init process wait function uses Cmd.Wait from os/exec. That Wait function can return a non-nil error if the init process does not complete successfully say if it exits with a non-zero exit code or is terminated.

If the cgroup's init process shares process namespace, all the other processes, if any, in the cgroup will not be killed, resulting in a process leak.

From libcontainer/process_linux.go:
```go
func (p *initProcess) wait() (*os.ProcessState, error) {
	err := p.cmd.Wait()
	if err != nil {
		return p.cmd.ProcessState, err
	}
	// we should kill all processes in cgroup when init is died if we use host PID namespace
	if p.sharePidns {
		signalAllProcesses(p.manager, unix.SIGKILL)
	}
	return p.cmd.ProcessState, nil
}
```

